From bcdf324d362b1f65db1737d81a93550c9a9b6bd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:17:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 52/54] HIP/RDNA3 one-column MMVQ: 2 rows per block for the
 K-quants (GGML_HIP_MMVQ_N1_ROWS)

One wave computes two rows of a ncols_dst == 1 launch of Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K, each row with the
lanes and partial-sum order of the one-row kernel (bitwise the same results): more weight
loads in flight per wave, activation loads shared by the rows. GGML_HIP_MMVQ_N1_ROWS=0
one row per block, =1|2|4 forces that many rows.

rocprofv3: shortconv in_proj 18.6 -> 12.9 us (466 -> 670 GB/s), expert gate+up 25.7 -> 24.3 us.
llama-bench tg128 -r 5, 3 interleaved rounds, same binary: off 4.610, 2 rows only for
launches >= 4096 blocks 4.567, 2 rows everywhere (taken) 4.509 ms/token (216.9 -> 221.8 t/s).
4 rows everywhere was slower (MMVQ 2624 vs 2487 us/token). Greedy md5 equal (LFM plain,
Qwen plain + MTP); test-backend-ops MUL_MAT 2476/2476, MUL_MAT_ID 931/931.
